The recursion-boundary probe found the main limitation: on a 998-element valid list, fresh K execution returns the complete 997-element derivative and the canonical Python does too, but the submitted CPython implementation raises `RecursionError`. I’m treating this as a documented normal-termination/exception bridge limitation—not a wrong returned-value witness—because the requested theorem is partial correctness; it materially prevents a clean PASS and universal CPython-equivalence claim.
